\section{Overview}
This appendix defines the zero-knowledge verification circuits used to enforce
Ex-Post Incentive Compatibility (EPIC) within the Cosmos-Harmony Runtime.
The circuits allow each region $i$ to prove compliance with incentive and
sovereignty constraints without revealing its private type vector
$\theta_i \in \Theta_i$.

\section{Commitment Scheme}
Each region commits to its private type using a post-quantum lattice-based
commitment:
\[
C_i = A \theta_i + r_i
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $A$ is a public randomness matrix derived from astrophysical entropy,
    \item $r_i$ is a high-entropy blinding vector.
\end{itemize}

\section{Constraint System}
Let the regional feasibility and incentive constraints be encoded as:
\[
g_i(\theta_i, u_{i,t}) \le 0,
\qquad
h_i(\theta_i, u_{i,t}) = 0
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $g_i$ encodes sovereignty bounds and operational limits,
    \item $h_i$ encodes EPIC incentive compatibility conditions.
\end{itemize}

These constraints define the arithmetic circuit:
\[
\mathcal{C}_i = (g_i, h_i)
\]

\section{Zero-Knowledge Proof Generation}
Each region produces a proof of knowledge:
\[
\pi_i = \text{ProveZK}(C_i, \mathcal{C}_i)
\]
such that:
\[
\text{VerifyZK}(C_i, \pi_i) = 1
\]
if and only if the committed $\theta_i$ satisfies all constraints.

\section{Circuit Structure}
The verification circuit consists of:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Commitment Consistency Gate}:
    \[
    A \theta_i + r_i = C_i
    \]
    \item \textbf{Feasibility Gates}:
    \[
    g_i(\theta_i, u_{i,t}) \le 0
    \]
    \item \textbf{Incentive Compatibility Gates}:
    \[
    h_i(\theta_i, u_{i,t}) = 0
    \]
    \item \textbf{Range and Bound Gates}:
    \[
    \theta_{i,\min} \le \theta_i \le \theta_{i,\max}
    \]
\end{enumerate}

\section{Security Properties}
The ZK-MPC protocol guarantees:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Zero-Knowledge}: No information about $\theta_i$ is leaked.
    \item \textbf{Soundness}: Invalid commitments cannot produce valid proofs.
    \item \textbf{Completeness}: Valid regional types always verify.
    \item \textbf{Post-Quantum Security}: Lattice commitments resist quantum attacks.
\end{itemize}

\section{Integration with MPC}
Once all proofs $\{\pi_i\}$ verify across the decentralized satellite mesh,
the MPC optimization horizon is evaluated over encrypted shares:
\[
u_t^* = \arg\min_{u_t \in \mathcal{U}_{\text{IC}}}
\sum_{\tau=t}^{t+H}
\left( \mathcal{L}(s_\tau, u_\tau) + \mathcal{P}(u_\tau) \right)
\]

\section{Conclusion}
This circuit specification provides the cryptographic foundation ensuring that
the Cosmos-Harmony Runtime remains incentive-compatible, privacy-preserving,
and globally verifiable.

